{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"1708f2a23423811ebbfa6cadb81a71721cd3b5d3c79dbacdee7f8e7ad4ffd074","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_0db10860239d68a0e1287cf136b8bdbee2199af72e15345106c15e44b3ccaa03","overall_assessment":"The paper is a technical contribution on hyperbolic attention networks. The supplied text does not contain a dedicated ethics, privacy, or broader-impact section. The datasets used (WMT14, CLEVR, Cora, CiteSeer) are standard public benchmarks, but the paper does not explicitly discuss data licensing, consent, or privacy compliance. The submission is anonymized as 'Anonymous authors' and marked 'Paper under double-blind review'. No evidence of plagiarism or dual submission is present in the text, though the authors acknowledge concurrent work.","paper_id":"rJxHsjRqFQ","paper_identity_sha256":"349fe71bf962813dd9cdc5571449a1fc786f2783cf411a1fc644f3b4f5d8fcb0","prompt_identity_sha256":"1e2f2cf92c4e8e2873c95a6d04d89ffc2968f6912f865c352c3382b61df4c00b","raw_response_sha256":"a5ccf03ede25f5ce6bc890b333e09268ffeea2b172b1d72c4cc74748358be97d","request_identity_sha256":"b02de7cb94bcd3c2ee154faafa670039b9b3f32402e139ac5dd8f34677fd8b4f","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"df91860328855e8d6e2486dc776d839f2ddc93d54a728050fb6215f0880a5c0a","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a specific section on ethics, fairness, or responsible AI. The work focuses on geometric improvements to attention mechanisms for tasks like machine translation and graph learning. There is no discussion of potential harms, bias, or dual-use risks associated with the proposed hyperbolic attention networks. Given the nature of the contribution (a methodological improvement on standard benchmarks), the absence of an ethics statement is not necessarily a critical flaw, but it represents a lack of explicit consideration of broader ethical implications.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-033"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes several standard public datasets: WMT14 for machine translation, CLEVR and Sort-of-CLEVR for visual question answering, and Cora/CiteSeer for graph transduction. The text does not provide explicit details on data licensing, consent, or privacy compliance for these datasets. While these are widely used benchmarks, the paper does not confirm adherence to specific data-use policies or mention any anonymization of data if it contained personal information (though WMT14 and CLEVR are typically non-sensitive). The lack of explicit licensing or consent documentation is a minor omission for a paper relying on public data.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper is submitted under double-blind review, as indicated by the header 'Anonymous authors' and 'Paper under double-blind review'. The text does not contain author names, institutional affiliations, or acknowledgments that would reveal the authors' identities. The references and citations are standard and do not appear to contain self-identifying information that would violate anonymity policies.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-008"],"review_text":"The paper acknowledges concurrent work by Cho et al. (2018) and Nickel and Kiela (2018), stating that they proposed similar methods in parallel. This is a standard practice for acknowledging related work and does not constitute dual submission or plagiarism. The text does not contain any evidence of textual overlap, uncredited reuse of material, or simultaneous submission to other venues. The originality of the hyperbolic attention mechanism appears to be clearly distinguished from prior work in the introduction and related work sections.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement or a checklist addressing societal considerations. There is no mention of IRB/ethics approvals, which is consistent with the use of public, non-human-subject datasets. The absence of a broader impact section is a common omission in technical papers of this era and venue, but it means the authors have not explicitly discussed the potential societal implications of their work, such as the efficiency gains in machine translation or graph learning.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"78f5cb9908c91d0d76f5e6fda228b4c46ca2cb915657730095e379b9be425b4a","paper_id":"rJxHsjRqFQ","paper_ordinal":103,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"a5ccf03ede25f5ce6bc890b333e09268ffeea2b172b1d72c4cc74748358be97d","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"rJxHsjRqFQ","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"a3f5fb33357c8011688b60991259886c6922e1e0d8c8a0993dbe5d221ee45cbd","request_identity_sha256":"b02de7cb94bcd3c2ee154faafa670039b9b3f32402e139ac5dd8f34677fd8b4f","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":875,"prompt_tokens":18881,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19756},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"b02de7cb94bcd3c2ee154faafa670039b9b3f32402e139ac5dd8f34677fd8b4f","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}